From 367ca6534fdcd30d1d513ee9b9e5c9217f085f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnikoopour <7692789+rnikoopour@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:38:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] dsv41: the prompt pass in steps (prefill_step), other
 streams' rounds between

prefillFn's body splits into fillOpen (placement, sequence, images, a kept
state's restore), one chunk a step, and the first token's draw. The model's
fill state is one stream's at a time on both ranks, so a step for another
stream than the last sends rank 1 its fill_begin and fill_images again and
sets them up here (fillResume). Rows read ahead for a fill's next chunk share
the Engram host's buffers with a round's reads: the read-ahead is joined at
each step's end and before every round on both ranks, and fillBegin drops
read-ahead rows (another fill may stand at the same position). A stream
released mid-pass frees its fill. prefillFn runs the steps back to back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
